    "description": "GlidePath Power Solutions develops, owns, and operates standalone battery energy storage projects across U.S. power markets. The platform serves utilities, grid operators, and other market participants by providing fast-response capacity and ancillary services that support reliability and renewable integration. Its model is asset-heavy, with projects developed, financed, and operated on a merchant or contracted basis depending on local market structure. Quinbrook describes GlidePath as a Chicago-based platform, and public disclosures tied to its 2018 wind acquisition cited a development pipeline exceeding 600 MW alongside broader distributed power activities. Quinbrook acquired GlidePath in 2017 through its low-carbon power strategy and has since used the platform as the core vehicle for its U.S. battery storage build-out.",
